     1,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\">Hi David (responded also to oSCR list), <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\">I think I posted a response to a similar question, which reminded me I need to integrate this updated version of the function to the package. For the time being, run this code:<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\">extract.rast2 &lt;- function(ss, rast, mult = 1, <a href=\"http://cov.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cov.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492175556000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Qx9VQlWz0lMrj-2gh_wVV\"><span style=\"color:black\">cov.name</span></a> = &quot;val.1&quot;,<br>                          buffer=NULL, method=&quot;simple&quot;, fun = mean){<br>  for(i in 1:length(ss)){<br>    tmpS &lt;- ss[[i]][, c(&quot;X&quot;, &quot;Y&quot;)] * mult<br>    r1 &lt;- raster::extract(rast, tmpS, buffer=buffer, fun = fun, na.rm=T)<br>    ss[[i]][, <a href=\"http://cov.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cov.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492175556000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Qx9VQlWz0lMrj-2gh_wVV\"><span style=\"color:black\">cov.name</span></a>] &lt;- r1<br>  }<br>  return(ss)<br>}<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\">if your raster is a single layer, the <a href=\"http://cov.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cov.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492175556000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Qx9VQlWz0lMrj-2gh_wVV\">cov.name</a> should be a single character you want to name the covariate in the ssDF. If it’s a stack/brick, then provide a vector of names and multiple columns will be generated. The mult argument is useful when you divide UTM coordinates by something to change from, e.g., m to km, in which case you’d do mult=1000. The buffer argument defined the buffer around the point to summarize the values, and the fun argument defines how to summarize.<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\">Note, though, that this function assumes the single raster or raster stack encompasses ALL state space points.<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\">(I guess I just wrote the help file </span><span style=\"font-family:Wingdings;color:#000066\">J</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\">)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\">Chris <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">spatialcapt...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">spatialcapt...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; <b>On Behalf Of </b>David Bernasconi<br><b>Sent:</b> Wednesday, December 18, 2019 1:20 PM<br><b>To:</b> Spatial Capture-Recapture &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">spatialcapt...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br><b>Subject:</b> Re: extract.raster() Clarification Question<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Also, after trying extract.raster() I have been getting the following warning:<u></u><u></u></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><div style=\"border:solid #bbbbbb 1.0pt;padding:0in 0in 0in 0in\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:#fafafa\"><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#660066\">Warning</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> messages</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">:</span></span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"><br></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#006666\">1</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">:</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> </span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#660066\">In</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> </span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#008800\">`[&lt;-.data.frame`</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">(</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#008800\">`*tmp*`</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">,</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> </span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">,</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> cov</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">.</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">name</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">,</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> value </span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">=</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> list</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">(</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> </span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">...</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> </span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">:</span></span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"><br><span>  provided </span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#006666\">1917</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> variables to replace </span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#006666\">1</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> variables </span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#006666\">1</span></span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br>Any ideas as to why raster values are not extracting would be greatly appreciated.<br><br><br>On Wednesday, December 18, 2019 at 11:04:28 AM UTC-5, David Bernasconi wrote:<u></u><u></u></p><blockquote style=\"border:none;border-left:solid #cccccc 1.0pt;padding:0in 0in 0in 6.0pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-top:5.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:5.0pt\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am hoping to get some clarification on how to extract raster values from different scaled raster data sets.<u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I would like to extract continuous values from my 30m resolution raster data to my 100m pixel resolution multi-session ssDF. Since I am going up in coarseness I would like the resulting ssDF pixel values to contain the mean raster value of the sampled 30m raster cells.<u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">If I wanted to do this for 1 raster data set, is the following correct?:<u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><div style=\"border:solid #bbbbbb 1.0pt;padding:0in 0in 0in 0in\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:#fafafa\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">ssDF</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">.</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">wetland_dist</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> extract</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">.</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">rast</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">ss</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">,</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> rast</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">,</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> mult </span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">=</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#006666\">1</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">,</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> cov</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">.</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">name </span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">=</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#008800\">&quot;DisttoWetland&quot;</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">,</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> func </span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">=</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> mean</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">)</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">If I have multiple continuous raster data sets, how should I  about extracting them to a multi-session ssDF?<u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Best,<u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">David <u></u><u></u></p></div></div></blockquote></div></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">-- <br>You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Spatial Capture-Recapture&quot; group.<br>To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">spatialcapturerec...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>To view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/spatialcapturerecapture/9e400bc7-de69-4d41-ac65-c4299d928b33%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/spatialcapturerecapture/9e400bc7-de69-4d41-ac65-c4299d928b33%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492175557000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2DiluXfcmOKveU4zOBX4M-\">https://groups.google.com/d/ms